   "screen": "What is digital media? Analogue versus digital",
   "title": "Figure 1.3.1 · An analogue signal and its digital version",
   "alt": "Two graphs of the same sound wave. Top, analogue: a smooth, continuous curve, like the groove in a vinyl record. Bottom, digital: the same wave measured at twelve regular moments. Each measurement is rounded to one of eight levels, 0 to 7, drawn as a column, and written underneath as a three-digit binary number, for example 100, 110 and 111. The stored file is just this list of numbers.",
   "caption": "The analogue signal changes smoothly with no gaps. The digital version keeps only measurements taken at regular moments, stored as binary numbers, which is why it can be copied and sent without loss.",
