   "screen": "The technology adoption lifecycle",
   "title": "Figure 1.4.1 · The adoption lifecycle and the chasm",
   "alt": "A bell curve divided into five groups from left to right: innovators 2.5 per cent, early adopters 13.5 per cent, early majority 34 per cent, late majority 34 per cent and laggards 16 per cent. The curve is split by a gap between early adopters and the early majority, labelled the chasm. A note explains that many products fail at this point because they never convince practical mainstream users (Geoffrey Moore). An arrow along the bottom shows time: groups further right adopt later.",
   "caption": "The bell curve is Rogers' diffusion of innovations. The gap after the early adopters is Moore's chasm: winning over the practical early majority is the hardest step.",
